* FD-01  Offset, output common mode, supply current, power, bias-pin voltage
* Spec 3.1.1.1, Fig. 26: inverting network R1 = R3, R2 = R4 (all {{R_NET}} ohm,
* gain -1), both input resistors driven by VIN = VCOM, operating point.
* Output offset = Vop - Von (0 for a symmetric design; the Monte Carlo run
* with corner tt_mm gives the random offset); input-referred
* VOS = (Vop - Von)/(1 + R2/R1); output common-mode error = (Vop + Von)/2 - VCOM.
* IOLP/IOLN: DC load current per output (0 A nominally; +/- for the spec 3.3.3 worst case).
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-6 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VI vi vcm 0
R1 vi inp {{R_NET}}
R2 inp outn {{R_NET}}
R3 vi inn {{R_NET}}
R4 inn outp {{R_NET}}
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp {{RL_NODE}} {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn {{RL_NODE}} {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
IOLP 0 outp DC {{IOUT_DC}}
IOLN 0 outn DC {{IOUT_DC}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
op
write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn) v(inp) v(inn) v(ibias) i(vdd) v(vcm) v(vcmpin)
.endc
.end
